    "_comment": "Full-toolset terrain (ADR-0043): domain-warped fbm base + a spine-driven ridged range to the WEST, hydraulically+thermally ERODED so the CDLOD surface (worldHalf 600 = size/2) carries real drainage. The VARIED peaks come from the low-frequency ridged-multifractal mountain layer (mountainHeight 150, mountainScale 0.0022 — big massifs + passes at different elevations, ~240 m peaks: stone band + snow caps), CONFINED to the range corridor by mountainAlongRange (the mountain mask is gated by the spine's cross falloff). That keeps the dramatic relief WEST of the origin while the metro core stays on gentle, buildable ground (headless probe: metro +-320 maxSlope 0.64, 0% steep) — mountainHeight everywhere (like cdlod.json) would spike the city. rangeWidth 240 keeps the falloff clear of the buildable core; the spine sits at x~=-555 (inside the +-600 mesh)."
